---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { services } from '../data/content';
import '../styles/pages.css';
---
<Base title="Prepare your project brief" description="Tell the story of your next business change. Prepare, review, copy, or download a project brief locally; this tool does not send an inquiry.">
  <section class="shell page-intro contact-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Reachly Studio / Your next step</p><h1 class="display page-title">A little context.<br /><em>A clearer conversation.</em></h1><div class="intro-tail"><span class="signal-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><p class="lede">Start with your business and what needs to change. You do not need to know the exact solution yet.</p></div></section>
  <section class="shell brief-layout section-space" aria-labelledby="brief-title">
    <aside class="brief-aside"><p class="eyebrow">Before you begin</p><h2 class="display" id="brief-title">Prepare it here.<br /><em>Keep it with you.</em></h2><div class="local-notice" id="local-notice"><strong>Local preparation only.</strong><p>There is no verified email, WhatsApp, or receiver connected to this tool. Your brief is not sent to Reachly. You can review it, copy it, or download it for sharing through a channel you have independently verified.</p></div><p>Entries stay in this page’s memory, with no automatic saving by the application. Leaving or refreshing may lose them. Do not include sensitive account or payment details.</p><a class="text-link" href="/privacy">How your brief is handled <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><ol class="brief-steps"><li><span>01</span> Describe your context</li><li><span>02</span> Review the prepared text</li><li><span>03</span> Keep a copy—nothing is sent</li></ol></aside>
    <div>
      <noscript><div class="local-notice"><strong>JavaScript is needed for the brief tool.</strong><p>No form submission is available. You can prepare the same information in a text document: your name, business, reply channel, service interest, and what needs to change. Nothing on this page sends it.</p></div></noscript>
      <form id="brief-form" aria-describedby="local-notice" autocomplete="off">
        <div id="brief-errors" class="error-summary" role="alert" tabindex="-1" hidden></div>
        <div class="form-pair">
          <div class="field"><label for="brief-name">Your name <span>(required)</span></label><input id="brief-name" type="text" required minlength="2" maxlength="100" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="brief-name-error" /><p class="field-error" id="brief-name-error"></p></div>
          <div class="field"><label for="brief-business">Business or project <span>(required)</span></label><input id="brief-business" type="text" required minlength="2" maxlength="160" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="brief-business-error" /><p class="field-error" id="brief-business-error"></p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="field"><label for="brief-reply">Reply email or phone <span>(required)</span></label><input id="brief-reply" type="text" required maxlength="160" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="brief-reply-hint brief-reply-error" /><p class="field-hint" id="brief-reply-hint">An email address or phone number with country code. Used only in your local brief; it does not request a reply.</p><p class="field-error" id="brief-reply-error"></p></div>
        <div class="field"><label for="brief-interest">What are you considering? <span>(optional)</span></label><select id="brief-interest" aria-describedby="brief-interest-hint"><option value="">I’m not sure yet</option>{services.map(service => <option value={service.slug}>{service.name}</option>)}</select><p class="field-hint" id="brief-interest-hint">A starting point, not a commitment to a package.</p></div>
        <div class="field"><label for="brief-message">What needs to change? <span>(required)</span></label><textarea id="brief-message" rows="7" required minlength="20" maxlength="4000" aria-describedby="brief-message-hint brief-message-error"></textarea><p class="field-hint" id="brief-message-hint">Tell us what your business does, what is getting in the way, and what a useful next step would look like. 20–4,000 characters.</p><p class="field-error" id="brief-message-error"></p></div>
        <div class="form-actions"><button class="button button--dark" id="brief-prepare" type="button" disabled>Review your brief <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button><button class="text-link clear-button" id="brief-clear" type="button" disabled>Clear brief</button></div>
        <p class="field-hint">Preparing a brief is not a booking, an inquiry submission, or an agreement.</p>
      </form>
      <section class="brief-review" id="brief-review" aria-labelledby="review-title" hidden><p class="eyebrow">02 / Review before keeping a copy</p><h2 class="display" id="review-title" tabindex="-1">Your brief is prepared.<br /><em>Nothing has been sent.</em></h2><label for="brief-preview">Prepared brief (read-only)</label><textarea id="brief-preview" readonly rows="16" spellcheck="false" aria-describedby="preview-hint"></textarea><p class="field-hint" id="preview-hint">Check your details. Copy or download when ready. If you change the fields above, review again to create an updated copy.</p><div class="form-actions"><button class="button button--dark" id="brief-download" type="button">Download TXT <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></button><button class="button" id="brief-copy" type="button">Copy brief</button><button class="text-link" id="brief-edit" type="button">Edit details ↑</button></div></section>
      <p id="brief-status" class="brief-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="shell contact-faq section-space"><p class="eyebrow">A few useful answers</p><h2 class="display">Before the conversation.</h2><details><summary>What if I do not know which service I need?</summary><p>Leave the interest as “I’m not sure yet.” Describe the business problem in your own words. A clear starting point is more useful than guessing at the technology.</p></details><details><summary>Can I send my brief from this page?</summary><p>No. This tool is local-only. It has no connected receiver and does not publish an unverified contact address. Keep a copy and share it only through a contact channel you have independently verified.</p></details><details><summary>Does preparing a brief establish a project or price?</summary><p>No. Scope, deliverables, timelines, pricing, access, and support need a separate agreement. The brief is a way to organize the conversation, not a quote or commitment.</p></details></section>
  <script>
    import '../scripts/contact.ts';
  </script>
</Base>
